    {
      "title": "Data Fetching Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Data Fetching Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Where Fetching Runs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`await fetch(url)` in an ==async== server component runs on the server",
                "Only rendered output ships: ==no client JS== for the fetch",
                "Fetch where the data is used; the same URL is ==deduplicated== per render",
                "Secrets stay on the server; never pass them as {red:props} to client components"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Source",
                "Deduped?",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`fetch(url)`",
                  "{green:Yes}, one render pass",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "DB / ORM call",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "wrap in `cache()`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "import { cache } from 'react'",
                "export const getUser = cache(",
                "  (id) => db.user.findUnique({ where: { id } })",
                ")"
              ],
              "note": "direct DB call, no API route"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Avoid Waterfalls",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sequential awaits make a ==waterfall==: each waits for the last",
                "Independent requests: start together with `Promise.all`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const [user, posts] = await Promise.all([",
                "  getUser(id),",
                "  getPosts(id),",
                "])"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why not fetch in useEffect?** Server fetch ships no JS and avoids a client waterfall.",
                "**Are ORM calls deduped?** No; wrap them in `cache()`.",
                "**Why Promise.all?** Sequential awaits create a waterfall."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Static vs Dynamic Rendering",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Static vs Dynamic Rendering",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Modes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Static}: HTML built at ==build time== (or on revalidate), served from cache",
                "{orange:Dynamic}: HTML built ==per request==",
                "Static: fastest, CDN-cacheable, can go ==stale==",
                "Dynamic: always fresh, costs ==server time== per request"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What Makes a Route Dynamic",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`cookies()` and `headers()`",
                "`searchParams` prop",
                "An ==uncached fetch== under your version's caching defaults"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'",
                "// or 'force-static'"
              ],
              "note": "route segment config forces a mode"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Check the Build",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:○} in build output = static",
                "{orange:ƒ} in build output = dynamic"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Layout trap",
              "text": "One request-time API in a ==layout== makes every child route **dynamic**."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Static or dynamic for a pricing page?** Static, since it is cacheable; revalidate to refresh.",
                "**How to spot a dynamic route?** ƒ in the build output."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Revalidation: Time-Based and On-Demand",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Revalidation: Time-Based and On-Demand",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Time-Based",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`fetch(url, { next: { revalidate: 60 } })` per fetch",
                "`export const revalidate = 60` per route",
                "==Stale-while-revalidate==: cached data is served, then refreshed in the background"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "sub": "within 60s",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cached",
                    "sub": "served at once",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "After 60s",
                    "sub": "still served stale",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Refresh",
                    "sub": "background",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. On-Demand",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`revalidatePath('/blog')` invalidates that route's cache",
                "Call it from a ==server action== or ==route handler==",
                "Tag the fetch, then `revalidateTag('posts')` hits every fetch with that tag"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "fetch(url, { next: { tags: ['posts'] } })",
                "",
                "// after the mutation succeeds",
                "await db.post.create(data)",
                "revalidateTag('posts')"
              ],
              "note": "revalidate after the write, not before"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compare and Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Time-based",
                "On-demand"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Setup",
                  "simple",
                  "needs a trigger"
                ],
                [
                  "Freshness",
                  "stale until timer",
                  "exact"
                ],
                [
                  "Trigger",
                  "clock",
                  "mutation or webhook"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Several revalidate values on one route: the ==lowest wins== for the page. Untagged fetches are never hit by `revalidateTag`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Next.js Caches",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Next.js Caches",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Four Caches",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cache",
                "Holds",
                "Lifetime"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Request Memoization==",
                  "identical `fetch` calls in one render",
                  "one request"
                ],
                [
                  "==Data Cache==",
                  "`fetch` results on the server",
                  "across requests and deploys"
                ],
                [
                  "==Full Route Cache==",
                  "HTML + RSC payload of static routes",
                  "built at build time"
                ],
                [
                  "==Router Cache==",
                  "visited route segments in the browser",
                  "one session"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Control and Invalidation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Data Cache: `revalidate`, tags, `cache: 'force-cache'` or `'no-store'`",
                "Full Route Cache: cleared when the Data Cache revalidates, or on {red:redeploy}",
                "Router Cache: back and forward are instant; ==`router.refresh()`== clears it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "fetch(url, { cache: 'force-cache' })",
                "fetch(url, { cache: 'no-store' })",
                "router.refresh()"
              ],
              "note": "Data Cache opt in, opt out, then clear the Router Cache"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Check Your Version",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Defaults change",
              "text": "Defaults for ==fetch caching== and the ==Router Cache== changed between releases. Check your version's docs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Streaming, Suspense and generateStaticParams",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Streaming, Suspense and generateStaticParams",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Streaming and Suspense",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Shell",
                    "sub": "sent first",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fallback",
                    "sub": "skeleton shows",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Slow part",
                    "sub": "streams in later",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Streaming== sends HTML in **chunks**: better time to first byte, faster feel",
                "Wrap a slow async server component in `<Suspense>`",
                "Only ==that subtree== waits; the rest renders at once",
                "`loading.tsx` = automatic Suspense around the **page**, instant on navigation"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "<Header />",
                "<Suspense fallback={<Skeleton />}>",
                "  <SlowFeed />",
                "</Suspense>"
              ],
              "note": "SlowFeed is an async server component"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. generateStaticParams",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Returns an array of params: pre-renders `/blog/[slug]` at ==build time==",
                "List only the **top pages**; the rest generate on first visit"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "export async function generateStaticParams() {",
                "  return [{ slug: 'a' }, { slug: 'b' }]",
                "}",
                "export const dynamicParams = false"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Unlisted param",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`dynamicParams = true` (default)",
                  "Rendered **on demand**"
                ],
                [
                  "`dynamicParams = false`",
                  "{red:404}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Suspense streams a ==slice==; `loading.tsx` wraps the **whole page**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes and Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes and Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Production Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Client `useEffect` fetch: adds a ==waterfall== and ships extra JS; use a server component",
                "Sequential `await`s: independent requests queue up instead of running together",
                "`cookies()` / `headers()` high in the tree: the whole route silently turns ==dynamic==",
                "Revalidating ==before== the mutation ends, or fetches without `tags`: stale data stays"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "const [user, posts] = await Promise.all([",
                "  getUser(),",
                "  getPosts(),",
                "])"
              ],
              "note": "start together, wait together"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "await db.post.create(data)",
                "revalidateTag('posts')"
              ],
              "note": "revalidate after the mutation; the fetch needs next: { tags: ['posts'] }"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cheat Sheet",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`revalidate = N`",
                  "{blue:timed} refresh"
                ],
                [
                  "`revalidatePath` / `revalidateTag`",
                  "{green:on demand} refresh"
                ],
                [
                  "`dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`",
                  "render {red:per request}"
                ],
                [
                  "`<Suspense>`",
                  "{purple:streams} slow parts"
                ],
                [
                  "`generateStaticParams`",
                  "==pre-renders== dynamic routes"
                ],
                [
                  "`router.refresh()`",
                  "clears the ==Router Cache=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "One request-time API high up makes every child route **dynamic**. Check the build output: ○ static, ƒ dynamic."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A root layout reads `cookies()` for a theme. Your blog page sets `revalidate = 60`. What does the build show?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Every child route is ƒ dynamic, rendered per request",
                "One request-time API in a layout makes the whole subtree dynamic",
                "Fix: read the cookie in a small component lower down"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Each fetch takes 1s. About how long does this page take, and how do you fix it?",
              "example_code": [
                "const a = await getUser()",
                "const b = await getPosts()"
              ],
              "a_bullets": [
                "About 2s: the second await waits for the first, a waterfall",
                "Run them together: `await Promise.all([getUser(), getPosts()])`",
                "That takes about 1s, the slowest request"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A server action calls `revalidateTag('posts')`, but the list never updates. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The list fetch carries no tag, so nothing matches",
                "Add `next: { tags: ['posts'] }` to that fetch",
                "Call revalidation after the mutation finishes"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
